    male|a||If a careful experiment finds no significant effect of health insurance on blood sugar, has it shown that insurance does nothing for blood sugar?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||That is the question Oregon left behind. In 2008 the state could afford about ten thousand more adults on Medicaid, about ninety thousand signed up, and it drew names by lottery.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lc4bxn'
    male|a||About two years later, researchers measured the blood sugar of some twelve thousand people who had entered the draw.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1djr9u1'
    male|a||Among those who lost, 5.1 percent had a glycated haemoglobin of 6.5 or more, the usual line for diabetes.:
